                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+category"} triangulated
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+categories"} homotopy categories
          %p
            For practical purposes it is, as usual, useful to enhance the data of the weak equivalences by further (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibration"}> co
            \-)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration"}> fibration
            auxiliary data. While there cannot be a suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2AAlg"} C*Alg
            itself (([Uuye 10]); there is however one on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/l.m.c.-C%2A-algebras"} l.m.c.-C*-algebras
            (
            %a{:href => "#JoachimJohnson07"}> JoachimJohnson 07
            )), there are suitable structures of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
            (
            %a{:href => "#Uuye10"}> Uuye 10
            ). These we discuss here. For actual
            = succeed "-structures" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+operator+algebras"} model structure on operator algebras
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %h3#categorytheoretic_preliminaries Category-theoretic preliminaries
          %p
            Write
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2AAlg"} C*Alg
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebras"} C*-algebras
            and
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%2A-algebra"} *-algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
            between them. We regard this as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo *
                  %mi Alg
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C^\ast Alg, \otimes)
            with the
            %em maximal
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+C%2A-algebras"} tensor product of C*-algebras
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi sep
                  %mo ↪
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo *
                  %mi Alg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast Alg_{sep} \hookrightarrow C^\ast Alg
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+topological+space"} separable
            = succeed "-algebras." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
          %p
            Write
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            for the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weakly+Hausdorff+topological+spaces"} weakly Hausdorff topological spaces
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            which forgets the
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%2A-algebra"} *-algebra
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo *
                  %mi Alg
                  %mo →
                  %mi Top
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  U \;\colon\; C^\ast Alg \to Top
                  \\,.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B \in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2AAlg"} C*Alg
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %mi Alg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^\ast Alg(A,B) \hookrightarrow Top(U(A), U(B)) \in Top
            %p
              be the set of
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace+topology"} subspace topology
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
              of the underlying topological spaces.
            %p
              This makes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %mi Alg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast Alg
              a
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2AAlg"} C*Alg
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              be
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Top(X,U(A)) \simeq U(C(X) \otimes A)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This defines a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/powering"} powering
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %mi Alg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast Alg
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mi cpt
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{cpt}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi X
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A^X \coloneqq C(X) \otimes A
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Uuye"}> Uuye, lemma 2.2
            )
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For every
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                      %mi Alg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in C^\ast Alg
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-functor"} hom-functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %mi Alg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %mi Alg
                    %mo →
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^\ast Alg(A,-) \;\colon\; C^\ast Alg \to Top
            %p
              preserves
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Uuye"}> Uuye, corollary 2.6
            )
          %h3#plain_homotopy_theory_of_algebras
            Plain homotopy theory of
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \coloneqq [0,1] \in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            for the standard topological
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval"} interval
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g \colon A \to B
              two morphisms in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2AAlg"} C*Alg
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+homotopy"} right homotopy
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta \colon f \Rightarrow g
              is a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta \colon A \to B^I
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi B
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi i
                                        %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi η
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi B
                              %mi I
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi g
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi B
                                    %mrow
                                      %msub
                                        %mi i
                                        %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; B
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{f}}\nearrow&amp; \uparrow^{\mathrlap{B^{i_0}}}
                    \\\
                    A &amp;\stackrel{\eta}{\to}&amp; B^I
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{g}}\searrow &amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{B^{i_1}}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; B
                    }
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Right homotopy is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [A,B]
              for the set of right homotopy-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
              of morphisms
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %mi Alg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [A,B] \simeq \pi_0 C^\ast Alg(A,B)
            %p
              These are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
              of a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %mi Alg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(C^\ast Alg)
          #HomotopyEquivalence.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Call a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon A \to B
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2AAlg"} C*Alg
              a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
              of
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ho
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                      %mi Alg
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(C^\ast Alg)
          #SchochetFibration.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Call a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon A \to B
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2AAlg"} C*Alg
              a
              %strong Schochet fibration
              if for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %mi Alg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \in C^\ast Alg
              the map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^\ast(D,f) \;\colon\; C^\ast(D,A) \to C^\ast(D,B)
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibration"} Serre fibration
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Schochet84"}> Schochet 84
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Uuye"} Uuye, def. 2.14, prop. 2.18
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              The category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2AAlg"} C*Alg
              equipped with weak equivalences being the homotopy equivalences of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyEquivalence"}
              and with fibrations being the Schochet fibrations of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SchochetFibration"}
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Schochet84"}> Schochet 84
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Uuye"} Uuye, theorem 2.19
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              The canonical functorial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+space+object"} path space object
              of a
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              in this structure is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^I
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega A = C_0((0,1), A)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Dually, interpreted as a space in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+topology"} noncommutative topology
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension"} suspension
              of the space that corresponds to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %h3#stabilization_at_the_compact_operators Stabilization at the compact operators
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒦
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo *
                  %mi Alg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K} \in C^\ast Alg
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebra"} C*-algebra
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+operators"} bounded operators
            on an infinite-dimensional
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+Hilbert+space"} separable Hilbert space
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              Say a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon A \to B
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2AAlg"} C*Alg
              is a
              %strong stable homotopy equivalence
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi 𝒦
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \otimes id_{\mathcal{K}}
              is a homotopy equivalence, def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyEquivalence"}
            %p
              Say
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a
              %strong stable Schochet fibration
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi 𝒦
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \otimes id_{\mathcal{K}}
              is a Schochet fibration, def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SchochetFibration"}
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              The category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2AAlg"} C*Alg
              becomes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
              with weak equivalences the stable homotopy equivalences and fibrations the stable Schochet fibrations.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Uuye"}> Uuye, prop. 2.24
            )
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p (…) kk-groups (…)
          %h3#kktheory KK-theory
          #KKEquivalence.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              Say a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon A \to B
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi sep
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast Alg_{sep}
              is a
              %strong KK-equivalence
              if for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi sep
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \in C^\ast Alg_{sep}
              the morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi KK
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi KK
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    KK(D,f) \;\colon\; KK(D,A) \to K(D,B)
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi KK
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KK
              is the
              = succeed "-category." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              The category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi sep
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast Alg_{sep}
              carries the structure of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
              whose weak equivalences are the KK-equivalences of def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KKEquivalence"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SchochetFibration"}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Uuye"}> Uuye, theore, 2.29
            )
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The various structures of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2AAlg"} C*Alg
            are discussed in
          %ul#Uuye10
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Otgonbayar+Uuye"}> Otgonbayar Uuye
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Homotopy theory for
                  = succeed "-algebras" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1011.2926"} arXiv:1011.2926
          %p using notions from
          %ul#Schochet84
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claude+Schochet"}> Claude Schochet
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topological methods for C∗-algebras. III. Axiomatic homology
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model categorical
            approach is presented in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Arne+%C3%98stv%C3%A6r"}> Paul Arne Østvær
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Homotopy theory of
                  = succeed "-algebras" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0812.0154"} arxiv/0812.0154
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://folk.uio.no/paularne/file0.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure presenting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
            not on
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\ast
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/l.m.c.-C%2A-algebras"} l.m.c.-C*-algebras
            is discussed in
          %ul#JoachimJohnson07
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Joachim"}> Michael Joachim
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Johnson"} Mark Johnson
              %em Realizing Kasparov’s KK-theory groups as the homotopy classes of maps of a Quillen model category
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0705.1971"}> arXiv:0705.1971
              )
